Here is the complete, production-ready codebase and architectural setup for your sustainable data center reference platform, designed for direct deployment to Cloudflare Pages with a native Cloudflare Pages Function + D1 (SQL) backend for newsletter subscriptions.

File Hierarchy

/
├── _headers                     # Security headers, CSP, and edge caching
├── robots.txt                   # Search engine crawl rules
├── sitemap.xml                  # XML sitemap for SEO indexation
├── schema.sql                   # Cloudflare D1 database setup schema
├── AI_GUIDE.md                  # Operational SOP manual for AI maintenance
├── styles.css                   # Responsive design system & dark/light themes
├── index.html                   # Pillar hub, instant search, and newsletter
├── facilities.html              # Renewable & zero-water facility directory
├── cooling-tech.html            # Thermodynamics & interactive PUE/WUE calculator
├── regulations.html             # International statutory mandates & legal matrix
├── baseload-nuclear.html        # Nuclear PPAs, SMRs, and FERC dockets
├── sources.html                 # Master bibliography of laws and research
└── functions/
└── api/
└── subscribe.js         # Cloudflare Pages edge function for D1 database

Backend: Cloudflare Pages Function & D1 Database

This setup requires no external third-party services. Form submissions are processed at the edge and stored directly in your Cloudflare D1 SQL database.

schema.sql

Run this once via the Cloudflare Dashboard or Wrangler CLI to create your subscribers table:

SQL
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS subscribers (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
  source_page TEXT DEFAULT 'index',
  created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_subscribers_email ON subscribers(email);

functions/api/subscribe.js

This serverless function intercepts POST /api/subscribe, verifies the email format, prevents duplicates, and writes directly to Cloudflare D1:

JavaScript
export async function onRequestPost(context) {
  const { request, env } = context;

  try {
    const contentType = request.headers.get("content-type") || "";
    let email = "";
    let sourcePage = "index";

    if (contentType.includes("application/json")) {
      const data = await request.json();
      email = data.email?.trim().toLowerCase();
      sourcePage = data.source || "index";
    } else if (contentType.includes("application/x-www-form-urlencoded")) {
      const formData = await request.formData();
      email = formData.get("email")?.toString().trim().toLowerCase();
      sourcePage = formData.get("source")?.toString() || "index";
    }

    const emailRegex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
    if (!email || !emailRegex.test(email)) {
      return new Response(
        JSON.stringify({ success: false, message: "Please provide a valid email address." }),
        { status: 400, headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" } }
      );
    }

    // Prepare statement to insert or ignore duplicate emails
    const statement = env.DB.prepare(
      "INSERT OR IGNORE INTO subscribers (email, source_page) VALUES (?, ?)"
    ).bind(email, sourcePage);

    const result = await statement.run();

    return new Response(
      JSON.stringify({
        success: true,
        message: result.meta.changes > 0 
          ? "Thank you for subscribing to sustainable infrastructure updates." 
          : "You are already subscribed to updates."
      }),
      { status: 200, headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" } }
    );
  } catch (error) {
    return new Response(
      JSON.stringify({ success: false, message: "A server error occurred. Please try again later." }),
      { status: 500, headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" } }
    );
  }
}


To connect D1 in Cloudflare Pages: In your Cloudflare dashboard, navigate to Workers & Pages → your project → Settings → Functions → D1 database bindings, and bind your database with the variable name DB.

