Here is the complete, expanded architecture and the updated build_zip.py builder script.

What Was Expanded & Redesigned

Elimination of Generic "AI Templates":

Removed glowing gradient cards, floating neon elements, and hollow buzzwords.

Adopted an editorial, institutional research layout (similar to CarbonPlan, Our World in Data, and IEEE Spectrum): crisp Swiss grid layouts, high-contrast readable typography, clean serif headings with tabular monospace figures, data tables, and formal statutory pull quotes.

Complete Unabridged Content Reinstated:

index.html: Restored the full Investigative Taxonomy (mapping Who, What, When, Where, Why, and How to SEC 10-K filings, NRC dockets, EPA permits, and NEPA reviews), the global power consumption forecasts (945 TWh by 2030), and the 4 Macroeconomic & Engineering Outlook vectors.

facilities.html: Restored full case studies for Moro Hub (Dubai), Microsoft's sealed AI builds (Phoenix & Mt. Pleasant with 172 dry cooling fans per building), Verne Global (Iceland geothermal), Start Campus SINES DC (Portugal 1.2 GW ocean cooling), and Google St. Ghislain.

cooling-tech.html: Restored the complete thermodynamics of latent heat vaporization, 1–5 million gallon daily campus consumption figures, blowdown wastewater dynamics, closed-circuit Direct-to-Chip (DLC) technology cooling systems (TCS), dielectric fluid specifications, elevated inlet temperature physics (>27
∘
C), and an expanded interactive calculator.

regulations.html: Restored the complete statutory review: Germany's EnEfG § 11 (PUE ≤1.2, 100% renewable power, 10%–20% mandatory district heat export, BAFA platform), Ireland's CRU LEU 80% additionality & 100% on-site storage mandates, Singapore's DC-CFA2 & GMDC:2024 standards, and EU EED Directive 2023/1791.

baseload-nuclear.html: Restored the comprehensive analysis of 5- to 7-year transmission queues, the Crane Clean Energy Center (TMI Unit 1) $1.6B restart, the landmark FERC Docket ER24-2172 Susquehanna order on ratepayer cost shifting, and Google's Kairos Power Hermes 2 SMR fleet.

Journalistic Images & Verified Attributions:

Integrated verified Wikimedia Commons and Copernicus satellite imagery for evaporative cooling, high-density compute aisles, solar park infrastructure, and commercial nuclear generation.

Cloudflare Compatibility:

Uses root _worker.js (Pages Advanced Mode). This bypasses the "Pages functions are not supported" error in Cloudflare's drag-and-drop dashboard, packaging both the static assets and the /api/subscribe edge endpoint in one step.

The Complete Builder Script: build_zip.py

Save the code below as build_zip.py and run python build_zip.py in your terminal or command prompt. It will immediately assemble the complete, publication-grade static site into greencompute-site.zip.

