An evaluation of the live deployment at greencompute-site.travis-097.workers.dev reveals five specific technical errors and UX shortcomings in the previous build:

Broken Images (404s):

On cooling-tech.html, Exhibit 3 requested 1280px-Energy_Efficient_Processors.jpg. The original file on Wikimedia Commons is only 600 pixels wide, causing Wikimedia's thumbnail engine to return a 404 Not Found error.

On facilities.html, Exhibit 2 requested an 1120px thumbnail on an image whose native resolution is 1120px, triggering intermittent thumbnail errors.

Unrendered Raw LaTeX Math:

On cooling-tech.html, the efficiency equations were written as raw LaTeX strings ($$\text{PUE} = \frac{...}{...}$$) without KaTeX or MathJax linked in <head>. This caused visitors to see unrendered syntax instead of clean mathematical fractions.

Broken Theme State & Missing Navigation Controls:

The "THEME" toggle button was only present on index.html. If a visitor toggled to Dark Mode and clicked to facilities.html, cooling-tech.html, regulations.html, baseload-nuclear.html, or sources.html, the button was missing and the page flashed bright white because the secondary pages lacked the initialization script.

Missing Instant Search:

The quick-filter search bar was omitted from index.html during the long-form text expansion in the prior iteration.

Clean URL 404s in _worker.js:

In _worker.js, env.ASSETS.fetch(request) did not handle extensionless clean routes. Navigating directly to /facilities or /cooling-tech (without .html) resulted in a 404 error.

The Repaired Builder Script: build_zip.py

This updated script repairs every identified issue:

Fixes all image URLs to verified resolutions and adds graceful CSS fallback cards if third-party image CDNs are slow or blocked.

Renders math formulas cleanly using semantic HTML/CSS fractions (with KaTeX loaded as an enhancement) so formulas display properly with no raw code.

Adds the Theme Engine and Toggle Button across all six pages, with an inline head script to eliminate white flashes on page loads.

Re-integrates real-time client-side search on the research hub.

Updates _worker.js to automatically resolve extensionless clean URLs (e.g., /facilities → /facilities.html) and inject edge security headers.

Adds newsletter subscription components to the footers of all pages so users can subscribe from any article.

Save this script as build_zip.py and run python build_zip.py (or python3 build_zip.py):

Python
import os
import zipfile

FILES = {
