      <h1>Global Architecture, Regulation, and Energy Systems of Advanced Data Centers</h1>
      <p class="lead">The rapid rise of artificial intelligence architectures and gigawatt-scale cloud clusters has transformed data centers from commercial real estate assets into utility-scale electrical and thermal infrastructure.</p>
      <p>As rack compute densities accelerate from legacy baselines of 5 to 10 kW toward 50 to 200 kW per rack, physical constraints around grid interconnection and municipal water supplies have forced a comprehensive engineering redesign. According to projections by the International Energy Agency, global data center electricity consumption will surpass 945 TWh by 2030. In the United States alone, data center demand is forecast to expand to between 325 and 580 TWh (74 to 132 GW) by 2028.</p>
