    <h2>Macroeconomic and Engineering Shifts</h2>
    <div class="editorial-grid" id="searchable-cards">
      <article class="article-card">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-amber">Regulatory Precedent</span>
          <h3>1. Scrutiny of Behind-the-Meter Colocation</h3>
          <p>Behind-the-meter generation allows hyperscalers to bypass 5- to 7-year transmission delays. However, FERC's November 2024 Susquehanna decision confirms that attempts to isolate large electrical loads from network transmission rates will face severe opposition from transmission owners and consumer ratepayer advocates.</p>
        </div>
        <p><a href="baseload-nuclear.html" style="color: var(--primary); font-weight: 600;">Inspect FERC Case Studies →</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="article-card">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-blue">Thermodynamics</span>
          <h3>2. The Water-Energy Decoupling Mandate</h3>
          <p>Public scrutiny over industrial water withdrawals is accelerating closed-loop Direct-to-Chip adoption. While closed loops eliminate on-site water consumption (WUE = 0.0 L/kWh), operators must elevate server fluid operating temperatures above 27°C to avoid heavy fan energy penalties in high-ambient climates.</p>
